# GraphLearn-for-PyTorch pin, read by gigl/scripts/install_glt.sh to build the GLT wheel.
#
# gigl-core compiles against GLT's C++ headers, so this commit MUST equal GIGL_GLT_COMMIT in
# gigl-core/GLT_PIN.cmake. Compiling against one commit while running against a wheel built from
# another silently corrupts shared-memory queue-size readings. tests/config_tests/dep_vars_check.py
# asserts the two agree and runs as part of the `precondition_tests` make target.
#
# See gigl-core/GLT_PIN.cmake for why the pin is stored in two files and how to bump it.
# WARNING: Ensure this matches GIGL_GLT_COMMIT in gigl-core/GLT_PIN.cmake ================================
GLT_COMMIT_SHA=88ff111ac0d9e45c6c9d2d18cfc5883dca07e9f9
# WARNING ====================================================================================================
